@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+---
+id: dl-006-rentals-of-3-days-or-more-get-10-percent-off-rounded-to-the-cent
+type: decision-log
+title: "Rentals of 3 days or more get 10 percent off, rounded to the cent"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The school wants to reward customers who stay longer. The brief says a rental of 3 days or more costs
+10% less than its full price, and that quotes and bookings both show the reduced total. Prices are
+integer euro cents (dl-002) and the full price is `dailyPrice` times the number of days (dl-001). A
+10% reduction of an integer number of cents can leave a fraction of a cent, so a rounding rule is
+needed.
+
+## Decision
+
+- A period of 3 or more days (`(end - start) / 24h >= 3`) is discounted. A period of 1 or 2 days is
+  priced as before. 3 days is inclusive.
+- The discounted total is the full price times 9/10, rounded half up to the whole cent. In integers:
+  `Math.floor((fullPrice * 9 + 5) / 10)`.
+- `quote` and `book` both return the discounted total in `total`. `Quote` and `Booking` keep their
+  fields; no field is added for the discount.
+- `availability` is unaffected, as it prices nothing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Example: 3 days at 1500 cents is 4500 full, 4050 discounted. A 2-day rental at 1505 cents is 3010 with
+  no discount. A 3-day rental at 1501 cents is 4503 full, 4053 discounted (4052.7 rounded up).
+- Rounding half up can leave the total up to half a cent above the exact discounted price, so it favours
+  the school by at most half a cent per rental. The result is deterministic and needs no floating-point
+  arithmetic.
+- Bookings made before this change keep their stored totals, since bookings are in memory only.
+- A later change to the threshold, the percentage or the rounding is a new decision.
