+---
+id: task-003-long-rental-discount-of-10-percent-for-3-days-or-more
+type: task
+title: "Long-rental discount of 10 percent for 3 days or more"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Rentals of 3 days or more cost 10% less than their full price. Quotes and bookings both show the reduced
+total. The rule and its rounding are recorded in `dl-006`.
+
+## Done
+
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: the new `long-rental discount` tests were written first and seen failing (5 of
+  them, all for the missing discount). They cover exactly 3 days, a longer rental, a 2-day rental at full
+  price, half-up rounding in both directions, and `book` returning the discounted total.
+- Two existing quote tests pinned the full price for 3 days, which the rule changes. The 3-day calendar
+  test now expects 4050, and the whole-days test now uses a 2-day rental, so it still checks full price.
+- `src/index.ts`: `discountedTotal` applies the discount in integers, `(price * 9 + 5) / 10`, from
+  `LONG_RENTAL_DAYS = 3`. `quote` and `book` both use it through `priceOf`. `availability` prices nothing
+  and is unchanged.
+- `README.md`: a bullet stating that `total` is the discounted price.
+- Design choices are recorded in `dl-006`.
+
+## Checks
+
+- `npm test` (`node --test`): 42 of 42 pass (37 pass before the implementation, 5 new discount tests failing
+  first).
+- `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` with a temporary TypeScript 5 install outside the project: no errors.
+
+## Open points
+
+- The brief does not say how a fraction of a cent is rounded. `dl-006` rounds half up to the cent, which is
+  a decision awaiting approval.
+- Bookings are in memory, so bookings made before this change keep their stored totals.
